      "subject": "Fix #423: Detect an empty RRCache before calling choice.",
      "body": "RRCache.popitem() relied on the choice function raising IndexError on an\nempty sequence, which is what the default random.choice does. Any other\nvalid choice function raised its own exception instead of KeyError, even\nthough the documented contract only requires choice to handle non-empty\nsequences. The other cache classes each detect emptiness on their own\nstructure first.",
      "source_files": [
        "src/cachetools/__init__.py"
      ],
      "test_files": [
        "tests/test_rr.py"
      ],
      "deleted_source": [],
      "lines_changed": 9,
